KG42.register("slice-clusters-181bb49f91bdfbc5ef603427",{"id":"17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v142-d-K002","paper":"17-exogenous_cost_allocation","title":"Conditional allocation, partner incentives, and settlement of exogenous network charges","source_pointer":"/clusters/68","node_ids":["COMP-166b347ab5fcd2a9","COMP-486b93e7e3eb4336","COMP-739917e3869e45a6","COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","COMP-f01e7a521b5470f4"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R005","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R008","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R004","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R003"],"visible_rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R005","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R008","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R004","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R003"],"suppressed_rule_refs":[],"edges":[{"global_edge_id":"S-bdced9f4178cba6b","source":"COMP-166b347ab5fcd2a9","target":"COMP-486b93e7e3eb4336","type":"links","assertion_ids":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R005::E::v141-c-R005-E001"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R005"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-b960eee1283d0d94","source":"COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","target":"COMP-166b347ab5fcd2a9","type":"links","assertion_ids":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E001"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R004"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-c6ee6885678aabaf","source":"COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","target":"COMP-166b347ab5fcd2a9","type":"links","assertion_ids":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E002"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R004"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-1c8733484f5fc703","source":"COMP-166b347ab5fcd2a9","target":"COMP-f01e7a521b5470f4","type":"links","assertion_ids":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E001"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R003"],"internal":false}],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"interface_annotations":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::theta_gamma_nm","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-gamma-nm","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e21","v141-b-g01-e26","v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E13","v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"The charge policy gives the applicable form of the charge coefficients, and the coordination chain provides the ex ante publication and conditional revision interface; they are combined only when the policy, time period, and transaction-direction conventions agree, and the three rates are not added together."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C005","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_d_nm"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E06"],"rationale":"The same distance-based charge policy explicitly incorporates distance into the charge and intends to encourage transactions with closer partners; this is a policy-incentive meaning, not a hard matching constraint guaranteeing selection of the nearest partner."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g02-E13"],"rationale":"The two chains respectively cover the uniform zonal charge example and the general differentiated zonal incentive, and belong to different conditional scopes of the same policy family; the uniform-charge formula cannot directly prove the differentiated effect in a specific high-price zone."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::theta_gamma_nm","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_gamma_n0"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T002","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-e21","v141-b-g01-e24"],"rationale":"The marginal and fixed terms of the same applicable charge are simultaneously used in the exogenous dispatch objective and in the settlement deduction; correspondence requires the same policy and time period, and the fixed term does not become a marginal incentive merely by entering the objective."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e25"],"rationale":"The separable charges in the objective connect to the charge collection reserved for the operator by each agent. Total cost, agents' net receipts and payments, and total collections are at different levels; these complete expressions cannot be judged as duplicate constraints, nor can full revenue adequacy be concluded on that basis."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-lambda-nm","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-p-nm"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_lambda_nm","v141-c-R008::x::x_p_nm","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e20","v141-b-g01-e24"],"rationale":"The final negotiated price and transaction quantity of the same transaction provide inputs to the payment relationship; any intermediate iteration does not automatically become a settlement result, and the stopping and reciprocity gaps remain associated with this interface."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-CN007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_p_nm","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e15","v141-b-g01-e24"],"rationale":"The partner permission scope limits transaction pairs that may have nonzero transactions and payment aggregation; permission does not mandate execution, exit must be permitted by the power bounds, and charge policy also does not automatically rewrite the partner set."}],"annotation_policy":"Original D connections are annotations, not additional S edges.","empty_after_chain_suppression":false});
